title: Entrance Initial Description
story: friendly-zoo
description: ADR-196 Phase 4 — entrance shows its first-visit (initial)
  description once, then the standard description on a re-look.
channels: room-description

---

# The opening's look at the entrance shows the first-visit-only flavor.
# This line sits above the first command, so it is a claim on the opening.
# The opening's row has no prose of its own to search, so the claim reads
# the channel the room's description travels on.
[CHANNEL: room-description, contains "Your family piles out of the car"]

# A typed look at the same room shows the STANDARD description, not the initial one.
> look
[OK: contains "wrought-iron gates"]
[OK: not contains "Your family piles out of the car"]
